<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siemowit III of Masovia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1320–1381</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Siemowit III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masovia">Masovia</a> was a Piast duke who reunited most of Masovia in the 1370s after the deaths of his relatives. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the Polish Crown, he issued a law code for the duchy and fostered its towns. After his death the lands were again divided among his heirs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siemowit-iii-of-masovia.jpg" alt="Siemowit III of Masovia" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous 1371 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Siemowit_III,_Duke_of_Masovia_1371.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
